[{"text":"\\[\\frac{k\\cdot p}{m^2 k^2.\\left((k-p)^2-m^2\\right)}-\\frac{k\\cdot p}{m^2 k^2.(k-p)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Using the option FeynAmpDenominator ->False we can specify that integrals without numerators should not be partial fractioned","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int = FAD[k, p - k, {k, m}] (SPD[q] + SPD[p, k])","anchor":"cb13","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{k\\cdot p+q^2}{k^2.(p-k)^2.\\left(k^2-m^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {k}]","anchor":"cb14","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{m^2+p^2+2 q^2}{2 m^2 k^2.\\left((k-p)^2-m^2\\right)}+-\\frac{1}{2 m^2 \\left(k^2-m^2\\right)}-\\frac{p^2+2 q^2}{2 m^2 k^2.(k-p)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb14-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {k}, FeynAmpDenominator -> False]","anchor":"cb15","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\frac{q^2}{k^2.\\left(k^2-m^2\\right).(p-k)^2}+\\frac{m^2+p^2}{2 m^2 k^2.\\left((k-p)^2-m^2\\right)}+-\\frac{1}{2 m^2 \\left(k^2-m^2\\right)}-\\frac{p^2}{2 m^2 k^2.(k-p)^2}","anchor":"cb15-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The extraPiece-trick is useful for cases where a direct partial fractioning is not possible","anchor":"cb15-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int = (SFAD[{{0, k . l}}, p - k] SPD[k, p])","anchor":"cb16","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{k\\cdot p}{(k\\cdot l+i \\eta ).((p-k)^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Here ApartFF cannot do anything","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {k}]","anchor":"cb17","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{k\\cdot p}{(k\\cdot l+i \\eta ).((p-k)^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb17-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Multiplying the integral with unity FAD[k]*SPD[k] we can cast into a more desirable form","anchor":"cb17-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int FAD[k], SPD[k], {k}] // ApartFF[#, {k}] &","anchor":"cb18","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{k^2}{2 (k\\cdot l+i \\eta ).((p-k)^2+i \\eta )}+\\frac{p^2}{2 (k\\cdot l+i \\eta ).((k-p)^2+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb18-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Here we need a second call to ApartFF since the first execution doesn’t drop scaleless integrals or perform any shifts in the denominators.","anchor":"cb18-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Other examples of doing partial fraction decomposition for eikonal integrals (e.g. in SCET)","anchor":"cb18-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int1 = SFAD[{{0, nb . k2}}, {{0, nb . (k1 + k2)}}]","anchor":"cb19","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta ).((\\text{k1}+\\text{k2})\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb19-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int1, {k1, k2}]","anchor":"cb20","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta ).(\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb20-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[ApartFF[SFAD[{{0, nb . k1}}] int1, SPD[nb, k1], {k1, k2}], {k1, k2}]","anchor":"cb21","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{(\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta ).(\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}-\\frac{1}{(\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta ).(\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb21-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int2 = SPD[nb, k2] SFAD[{{0, nb . (k1 + k2)}}]","anchor":"cb22","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}}{((\\text{k1}+\\text{k2})\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb22-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int2, {k1, k2}]","anchor":"cb23","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}}{(\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb23-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[ApartFF[SFAD[{{0, nb . k1}}] int2, SPD[nb, k1], {k1, k2}], {k1, k2}]","anchor":"cb24","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}}{(\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{nb}+i \\eta )}\\]","anchor":"cb24-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"If we are working with a subset of propagators from a full integral, one should better turn off loop momentum shifts and the dropping of scaleless integrals","anchor":"cb24-1","section":"Examples"}]